{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WWM5YxP8awfCxaWNjJZrwU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found it! The work buffer sizing at line 626-631 has a critical issue:\n\n```rust\nlet max_work_size = if total_rounds > 2 {\n    if precompute_m_env {\n        (total_leaves >> (2 + GKR_WINDOW_SIZE)).max(1 << GKR_WINDOW_DEFAULT_MIN_N)\n    } else {\n        total_leaves >> 2\n    }\n} else {\n    0\n};\n```\n\nWhen `precompute_m_env` is true (which it is even when we change MIN_N), the work buffer size is computed as:\n\n\n- `(total_leaves >> 5).max(1 << 22)`\n\nThe hardcoded `1 << 22` minimum was designed for FoldEval fallback rounds, but increasing MIN_N to 24 means FoldEval now handles rem_n values up to 23, requiring a larger work buffer than what's currently allocated.\n\nThe issue is that `GKR_WINDOW_DEFAULT_MIN_N` is a compile-time constant set to 22, so even when MIN_N is changed via environment variable to 24, the work buffer sizing still uses 22. For FoldEval rounds at rem_n=23, the post-fold pq data needs `2^24` elements, but the buffer is capped at `2^22`, which isn't enough.\n\nFor APC 300 segments with `2^27` total leaves, the work buffer maxes out at `2^22`, but when rem_n=23 the pq_size starts at `2^24` and after folding becomes `2^23`—still larger than what's allocated. The fix is to make the work buffer sizing use the actual MIN_N value from the environment variable instead of just the compile-time constant.\n\nThe issue is that `max_work_size` uses `GKR_WINDOW_DEFAULT_MIN_N` (the const), while the runtime computation calls `precompute_m_min_n()` which reads the env var, creating a mismatch. I need to read the env var earlier, before the buffer is sized, so the runtime value gets used for allocation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2035,"cache_read_input_tokens":73638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2035},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44c7b500-938c-4db0-96c2-3c0becdebec3","uuid":"764771ad-74a3-42e1-8c8f-6f6d610c87a8"}
