{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015sdVRxcDqR9jeEwZ69VsDG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Disabling PrecomputeM entirely: LogUp GKR 446ms (+79ms worse), STARK excl trace 1200ms (+87ms worse).\n\nNow this is interesting. The data shows that PrecomputeM is significantly beneficial — disabling it adds 79ms to GKR. So the question becomes: can we make PrecomputeM work for even more layers by *lowering* MIN_N?\n\nCurrently MIN_N=22, which means layers with rem_n < 22 use FoldEval. What if we lower it to 20 or 18? That would use PrecomputeM for more layers.\n\n\nBut I need to check the actual constraints — the diagnostic showed app segments have layers ranging from rem_n=0 to rem_n=26, and there's also a min_blocks check that might be blocking smaller layers from using PrecomputeM even if I lower MIN_N. Let me examine what that check is actually doing.\n\nFor rem_n=21 with w=3, I'm walking through the calculation: tail_n becomes 18, which gives k=262144, and with a target of 1024 blocks, the desired tile size is 256. After clamping, tail_tile stays at 256, yielding 1024 tail blocks — which passes the min_blocks threshold of 64.\n\nTesting smaller values of rem_n with the same w=3, I see that rem_n=20 produces 512 tail blocks, rem_n=18 produces 128, and rem_n=15 would produce fewer still, but all continue to pass the threshold check.\n\nHowever, once I get down to rem_n=15, the calculation shows only 16 tail blocks, which falls below the 64-block minimum and forces a fallback to FoldEval. This means lowering MIN_N has a hard ceiling around rem_n=15 before the min_blocks constraint kicks in.\n\nFor the APC 300 application with 27 rounds, I'm seeing that adjusting MIN_N could extend PrecomputeM coverage—setting it to 20 adds a couple extra layers per segment, 18 adds four more, and 16 would add six—but the min_blocks check will ultimately limit how far down we can go.\n\nI should also verify the rounds_left constraint isn't blocking anything. Looking at the calculation for various rounds in that range, the constraint appears satisfied across the board, so that's not the limiting factor here.\n\nNow I'm testing a few specific MIN_N values to see which ones actually work.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":243,"cache_read_input_tokens":83791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":243},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44c7b500-938c-4db0-96c2-3c0becdebec3","uuid":"7be80787-7515-452c-a0bc-0fd67dc339e6"}
