{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KcU8P6aW8PMH1vTwXznL3n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014YdnuayQ3CWctky9th3HZj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git -C /home/georg/stark-backend commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nFix GKR PrecomputeM work buffer sizing to use runtime MIN_N\n\nThe work buffer for GKR fractional sumcheck used the compile-time\nconstant GKR_WINDOW_DEFAULT_MIN_N (22) instead of the runtime\nprecompute_m_min_n value when computing the maximum buffer size.\nWhen SWIRL_CUDA_GKR_PRECOMPUTE_M_MIN_N was set higher than 22 via\nenv var, FoldEval fallback rounds at rem_n > 22 needed larger work\nbuffers than 2^22 elements, causing cudaErrorIllegalAddress.\n\nMove the env var reads before the buffer sizing computation and use\nthe runtime value. No change to default behavior (MIN_N defaults\nto 22, same as the constant).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit the implementation change"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":156,"cache_read_input_tokens":101344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":156},"output_tokens":61,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44c7b500-938c-4db0-96c2-3c0becdebec3","uuid":"bd4a1745-6f73-4a43-8459-81c1d09ee127"}
